.el .ds Aq '
.TH hipfire-diffusion 1  "hipfire-diffusion "
.SH NAME
hipfire\-diffusion \- Import and inspect diffusion models stored as .hfq artifacts
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBhipfire\-diffusion\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Import and inspect diffusion models stored as .hfq artifacts
.PP
Runnable .hfq diffusion artifacts currently use the native UNet-family CPU
reference path for CLIP text conditioning, UNet denoising, VAE decode, and VAE
encode for img2img. ROCm preflight validates planned device buffers plus
individual kernels for model-input scaling, classifier-free guidance, Euler
scheduler updates, residual tensor add, NCHW channel-bias add, NCHW/BSC layout
transforms, f32 NCHW Conv2D, f32 NCHW GroupNorm, SiLU, nearest-neighbor
upsample, f32 dense linear projection, f32 LayerNorm, f32 row softmax, f32 3D
scaled-dot-product attention, f32 CLIP causal self-attention, GeGLU gate, and
RGB conversion, but full generation is not routed through a GPU UNet runtime
yet. The runtime accepts Q4F16_G64, f16, bf16, f32, Q8F16, Q4_K, HFQ4G128,
HFQ4G256, and HFQ6G256 tensor payloads even when the artifact weight_format
records a future quantized format such as oq4; OQ/MQ/HFP and other packed
payloads still require a matching diffusion dequantizer/HIP runtime before they
can generate images.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
hipfire\-diffusion\-import(1)
Convert a Diffusers snapshot or single\-file checkpoint into a Hipfire .hfq artifact
.TP
hipfire\-diffusion\-inspect(1)
Inspect a diffusion .hfq artifact and print its server\-facing summary
.TP
hipfire\-diffusion\-preflight(1)
Plan HIP diffusion buffers and optionally run a ROCm device preflight
.TP
hipfire\-diffusion\-txt2img(1)
Generate PNG images directly from a diffusion .hfq artifact
.TP
hipfire\-diffusion\-img2img(1)
Generate PNG images from init images with a diffusion .hfq artifact
.TP
hipfire\-diffusion\-smoke(1)
Run an end\-to\-end diffusion admission smoke and validate output PNGs
.TP
hipfire\-diffusion\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
